Ep188 — The Source Speaks

The doors of the City Hall chamber swing open.

The room falls silent — scientists, journalists, council members, all turn as one.

Diana Reyes stands frozen at the podium, a single sheet of paper in her hand.

And in the doorway, Folana Lanez steps through.

Water still drips from her fingertips. Violet light traces faint lines through the air around her.

She does not speak at first. She just stands there — letting them see her.

The frequency is not in the pipes anymore. It is not in the bridge cables or the subway rails.

It is standing in the doorway of the City Hall chamber, looking at the woman who has been speaking for her all this time.

And when she finally does speak, her voice is quiet — but the whole room hears it.

"You asked what it means. I'm here to show you."

The delegate and the source. Face to face at last.

This is Ep188. The Source Speaks.
